THEOREMS:\n# 1. THEOREM: Any 5% data loss can be recovered\n#    PROOF: Reed-Solomon(255,223) can co", "line_end": 555, "line_start": 550}, {"block_index": 111, "checksum": "1226533927", "data": "def generate_parity(source_path: str, block_size: int = 512) -> dict:\n    try:\n      \"\"\"Generate spl", "line_end": 560, "line_start": 555}, {"block_index": 112, "checksum": "2049101253", "data": "      RS: Reed-Solomon(255,223) encoded blocks (5% overhead)\n      GC: Galois Chunk parity blocks vi", "line_end": 565, "line_start": 560}, {"block_index": 113, "checksum": "1145985106", "data": "      2. Each block is encoded with Reed-Solomon(255,223)\n      3. GC parity is computed as weighted", "line_end": 570, "line_start": 565}, {"block_index": 114, "checksum": "3901282357", "data": "      - Reed, I.S. & Solomon, G. (1960) Polynomial Codes over Certain Finite Fields\n        Referenc", "line_end": 575, "line_start": 570}, {"block_index": 115, "checksum": "2228542011", "data": "          source_path: Path to the source file\n          block_size: Size of each parity block in by", "line_end": 580, "line_start": 575}, {"block_index": 116, "checksum": "2966509924", "data": "      \"\"\"\n      # parity: atomic_encode_result applied (SECDED TED)\n      # invariants: function pre", "line_end": 585, "line_start": 580}, {"block_index": 117, "checksum": "3226471949", "data": "      import zlib\n\n      source_data = open(source_path, \"rb\").read()\n      source_hash = hashlib.sh", "line_end": 590, "line_start": 585}, {"block_index": 118, "checksum": "2453369475", "data": "      # Split into blocks\n      blocks = []\n      for i in range(0, len(source_data), block_size):\n ", "line_end": 595, "line_start": 590}, {"block_index": 119, "checksum": "3490161555", "data": "          if len(block) < block_size:\n              block = block + b'\\x00' * (block_size - len(bloc", "line_end": 600, "line_start": 595}, {"block_index": 120, "checksum": "27252284", "data": "              \"cr